# Portable JVM options - these have to work both in the container and on a developer machine.
#
# Three options used to live here and have moved to the container, because they are container-only
# and one of them is fatal elsewhere:
#   -XX:+UseContainerSupport   Linux-only. On macOS HotSpot it is an unrecognized option and the
#                              JVM refuses to start, so no native run was possible at all.
#   -XX:MaxRAMPercentage=75.0  only meaningful alongside the flag above.
#   -DAppLogDir=/logs          /logs exists in the image and nowhere else. log4j2.xml now falls
#                              back to a relative "logs" directory when this is unset.
# docker-compose.yml passes all three through JVM_ARGS, which the Liberty image already honours.

# Chooses the security wiring: 'production' and 'qa' register the real WebSEAL header filter,
# 'local', 'dev' and 'fit' register the developer stub. A native run has no proxy in front of it,
# so it needs the stub; the container overrides this through JVM_ARGS.
-Dspring.profiles.active=local

-Djava.awt.headless=true
-Dfile.encoding=UTF-8
-Duser.timezone=America/New_York

# Fail fast on an out of memory condition rather than limping on in a state nothing can trust.
-XX:+ExitOnOutOfMemoryError
